sections.body:
You can join text with `+`, but a **template string** is much easier. A template string is written with **backticks** instead of quotes, and variables go inside `${...}`:

```js
const pilot = "Alex";
const planet = "Mars";
console.log(`Hello ${pilot}, target: ${planet}!`);
// Hello Alex, target: Mars!
```

You can put calculations inside `${...}` too: where you write `${3 + 4}`, the output shows `7`.

examples.code:
const ship = "Eagle";
const speed = 40000;
console.log(`${ship} is flying at ${speed} km per hour.`);

const message = "  Alert: Fuel Low  ";
const clean = message.trim();
console.log(clean.toUpperCase());
console.log(clean.includes("Fuel"));
console.log(clean.length);

